{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"kind\":\"final\",\"decision\":\"answer\",\"answer\":1220,\"evidence\":[\"receipt-1\"],\"confidence\":0.9,\"status\":\"SUPPORTED\",\"reason\":\"Dynamic programming counts binary words of length 14 avoiding 000 and 111\"}","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 14 that avoid forbidden substrings \"000\" and \"111\". So no three consecutive same bits. Count sequences of length n with no run of 3 same bits. This is classic recurrence. Let a_n be number of sequences length n ending with run of length 1 of some bit, b_n ending with run length 2. Actually we need states: last bit value and run length 1 or 2. But since bits symmetric, we can count total sequences. Let A_n = number ending with run length 1, B_n = number ending with run length 2. For n=1: A_1=2 (0 or1), B_1=0. Transition: If we have run length1, we can add same bit to get run length2: B_{n+1} += A_n. Or add opposite bit to get run length1: A_{n+1} += A_n. If we have run length2, we cannot add same bit (would be 3), so must add opposite bit to get run length1: A_{n+1} += B_n. So recurrence: A_{n+1}=A_n + B_n, B_{n+1}=A_n. Base: A1=2,B1=0. Compute up to n=14. Let's compute quickly.\n\nn=1: A=2,B=0,total=2\nn=2: A2= A1+B1=2+0=2; B2= A1=2; total=4\nn=3: A3= A2+B2=2+2=4; B3= A2=2; total=6\nn=4: A4= A3+B3=4+2=6; B4= A3=4; total=10\nn=5: A5=6+4=10; B5=6; total=16\nn=6: A6=10+6=16; B6=10; total=26\nn=7: A7=16+10=26; B7=16; total=42\nn=8: A8=26+16=42; B8=26; total=68\nn=9: A9=42+26=68; B9=42; total=110\nn=10: A10=68+42=110; B10=68; total=178\nn=11: A11=110+68=178; B11=110; total=288\nn=12: A12=178+110=288; B12=178; total=466\nn=13: A13=288+178=466; B13=288; total=754\nn=14: A14=466+288=754; B14=466; total=1220\n\nThus answer 1220. Provide final JSON."}}],"created":1790945445,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":